   "id": "digital-timer",
   "title": "Digital timer application",
   "page": 6,
   "description": "A retriggerable one-shot. The RC network on pins 1 to 3 runs the oscillator; AR and MODE are at ground, so power-on reset is active and the timer is in single-cycle mode, and Q/Q SEL is at VDD so Q is high after a reset. A positive pulse of width tMR on MR clears the counters and the latch; Q goes high and stays high until the stage chosen by A and B has counted, then goes low until the next pulse. The output pulse lasts t + tMR. Its accuracy is that of the clock; for better accuracy an external clock can drive pin 3, with pins 1 and 2 left as outputs. After first power-up Q is high for one pulse-width before the timer is ready.",
